Architecture plan for Issue #222: Use the logo's sail shape for the favicon

Scope and module structure
- Static asset layer: update public/favicon.svg and public/images/ideavibes-mark.svg to the same sail-only Ideavibes mark: no wordmark, no red dot, no background.
- Binary favicon asset: regenerate public/favicon.ico from the same sail-only source so browser ICO fallback matches the SVG favicon and is not stale.
- Template/layout layer: keep rust-backend/templates/layout.html favicon links unchanged; the issue explicitly says the existing /favicon.ico and /favicon.svg links should remain as-is.
- Test layer: update rust-backend/src/html/mod.rs tests to assert the shared layout includes the /favicon.svg link.

Dependencies between issues
- This batch contains only Issue #222.
- It depends on the previous hosted header/footer logo behavior staying intact: do not change the hosted header/footer logo URL introduced by Issue #220.

Key design decisions
- Product branding is Ideavibes, exactly as named in the issue.
- Use a repo-native SVG edit for the sail mark instead of generating a new wordmark or adding background/red-dot elements.
- Treat the SVG sail mark as the source of truth, and regenerate favicon.ico from it.
- Limit code changes to tests/layout assertions; no routing, API, database, auth, storage, or environment behavior changes are needed.
